       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of 3,200 mg for adults. A single 1600 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose. At that level the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day total)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), which is a common anti-inflammatory dose\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me and include a note on the clinical rationale. I'll then enter it as written. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
